     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Bases and ranges",
     "md": "Place values in binary are powers of 2. An n-bit **unsigned** integer ranges from 0 to 2ⁿ - 1 (8 bits: 0 to 255). Hexadecimal groups four bits: 1011 0111 = B7 = 11 x 16 + 7 = 183. Use hex to write long binary numbers compactly."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Two's complement",
     "md": "In n-bit two's complement the leftmost bit has a **negative** weight (-128 in 8 bits). To negate a number: flip all bits and add 1. -45: 45 = 00101101, flipped 11010010, plus 1 gives **11010011**. Range for 8 bits: -128 to +127. Subtraction is addition of the negative."
    },
